 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No ruins, destruction or people drawn. Rain for «السماء مدرارا» (a blessing given as respite), a book for the hypothetical «كتابا في قرطاس». Their saying «إن هذا إلا سحر مبين» is glossed only as «ظلم وبغي». As-Sa'di's first-person «إهلاكنا» not used. STAGING v4: 6: the garden is empty while the past generations are named; a nation (uncountable) walks in on 6:9 (established in the land), rain on 6:17-6:19, the land greening on 6:19 and a river plate on 6:21 (both tafsirs: rain and rivers; As-Sa'di: crops and fruits); they turn on 6:22 (As-Sa'di: they did not give thanks) and leave on 6:24, well before 6:25; per the caution no ruin or destruction is drawn, only the empty garden and drifting leaves; another generation walks in on 6:27. 7 (a counterfactual book on parchment) stays ambient with no book plate, so nothing hypothetical is drawn."
 },
